WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.099 --> 00:00:12.469
Did you know &nbsp;there is a country in South
America where most of its population are of

00:00:12.469 --> 00:00:16.390
Indian origin and where the official language
is English?

00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:23.730
If you don´t know which country I´m talking
about, don’t worry, because this is one

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:28.369
of the least known countries in the region
and, to be fair, the media doesn’t really

00:00:28.369 --> 00:00:30.279
pay much attention to it.

00:00:30.279 --> 00:00:33.000
So, a small, little-known country, the media
don’t talk much about…

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:38.710
Well those sound like the perfect ingredients
for a VisualPolitik video!

00:00:38.710 --> 00:00:45.429
We are talking about Guyana, an old British
colony who didn’t get independence until

00:00:45.429 --> 00:00:46.569
1966.

00:00:46.569 --> 00:00:51.589
Interestingly, at the moment of independence,
both the government and popular opinion was

00:00:51.589 --> 00:00:55.929
generally in favour of turning Guyana into
a socialist country.

00:00:55.929 --> 00:01:00.930
It was this mindset which gave the country
its pinto-esque official name: the COOPERATIVE

00:01:00.930 --> 00:01:02.239
Republic of Guyana.

00:01:02.239 --> 00:01:05.150
But, let’s focus on the country today.

00:01:05.150 --> 00:01:09.510
Guyana is one of the poorest countries in
South America.

00:01:09.510 --> 00:01:16.909
It has crime and violence rates that are some
of the highest in South America…

00:01:16.909 --> 00:01:18.340
And that’s saying a lot.

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:22.670
In fact, if Guyana is know for anything, it
would be for its place in the international

00:01:22.670 --> 00:01:24.280
supply of cocaine…

00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:30.659
Oh, and also for having one of the highest
suicide rate in the world.

00:01:30.659 --> 00:01:35.100
With all this information, you’d be forgiven
for being less than optimistic about the future

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:36.570
of this caribbean country.

00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:40.320
But, they may get lucky in the near future.

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:48.560
A NEW OIL POWER
All the signs are point to Guyana becoming

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:49.700
an oil power.

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:55.020
For the time being, this small republic, with
a population of about 750,000 inhabitants

00:01:55.020 --> 00:02:00.140
has already got the attention and dollars
of multinational companies such as Exxon or

00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:01.829
Hess Co.

00:02:01.829 --> 00:02:10.069
In fact, after several years exploring the
area, on the 13th January 2017, these two

00:02:10.069 --> 00:02:14.870
powerful oil companies announced the discovery
of what they think could be one of the most

00:02:14.870 --> 00:02:18.970
significant oil and gas reserves found for
decades.

00:02:18.970 --> 00:02:23.440
Oil reserves have been found in deep waters,
in the sea mantle, under the coastal waters

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:24.440
of Guyana.

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:28.580
Early calculations estimate that the amount
of oil which can be exploited in the country

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:35.500
is no less than 4,000 million barrels and
many experts affirm this could be a much larger

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:36.500
quantity.

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:41.390
So, it seems that this country holds a huge
fortune just off its shores, but the question

00:02:41.390 --> 00:02:45.140
really is - how much is this all really?

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:49.700
Considering the price of oil nowadays, we
are talking about roughly $200 billion.

00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:55.760
So, leaving other natural resources aside,
only petrol, would result in the equivalent

00:02:55.760 --> 00:02:57.870
of $250,000 per citizen.

00:02:57.870 --> 00:03:02.870
And it’s important to note that the oil
reserves could be much bigger than the early

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:05.490
calculations indicate.

00:03:05.490 --> 00:03:12.510
Now, it is true that oil exploitation is expensive
and requires enormous investment, but this

00:03:12.510 --> 00:03:17.870
could still be the first step in a new era
of prosperity for Guyana.

00:03:17.870 --> 00:03:22.340
So far the oil companies I have mentioned:
Exxon Mobil and Hess have committed to investing

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:27.150
$900 million a year in Guyana, over the next
few years.

00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:31.170
The government is investing too, with plans
to start exporting oil in 2020.

00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:36.570
This means Guyana could be on the cusp of
beginning one of the greatest economics developments

00:03:36.570 --> 00:03:39.980
that South America has ever seen.

00:03:39.980 --> 00:03:51.460
Yes, Guyana, that poor, violent country, could
become the kind of country which other people

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:56.180
in South America who are unemployed might
look at and think: “I want to change my

00:03:56.180 --> 00:03:58.090
life, I want opportunities…”

00:03:58.090 --> 00:04:03.880
Guyana could become that big hope for many
people in South America.

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:09.790
Nevertheless, before they start packing, we
have to say that it won’t be that easy.

00:04:09.790 --> 00:04:17.509
The road ahead is fraught with difficulties...

00:04:17.509 --> 00:04:21.720
CONFLICT WITH VENEZUELA
Much of the oil exploration is happening in

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:23.940
waters which are claimed by Venezuela.

00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:27.750
And, the part they have claimed is not exactly
small...

00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:31.870
Maduro´s country considers the region known
as Guyana Esequiba to be theirs.

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:38.000
And this region represents more than 70% of
Guyana´s surface!

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:42.500
So essentially Venezuela is claiming the entire
country as their own!

00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:47.370
And if this wasn’t bad enough, another area
which makes up 7% of its territory is claimed

00:04:47.370 --> 00:04:49.430
by their neighbours in Surinam.

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:53.600
If their neighbours had their way Guyana would
have been carned up and split between them

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:54.960
long ago.

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:58.880
The thing is, this conflict over territory
seemed to have been forgotten for years.

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:03.350
This was likely a consequence of the good
relations that the government kept with Cuba...

00:05:03.350 --> 00:05:08.250
a country that holds a lot of influence over
this part of the world.

00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:14.960
It was also likely because Venezuela wanted
the support of organizations such as CARICOM,

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:17.380
the Caribbean Community, of which Guyana is
a member.

00:05:17.380 --> 00:05:22.810
So, you might be wondering, is Guyana a Caribean
country, or is it a South American country?

00:05:22.810 --> 00:05:28.080
Well it’s sort of both... geographically
speaking the country is South American.

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:32.850
But, politically, socially, and culturally
speaking, Guyana is a Caribbean country.

00:05:32.850 --> 00:05:38.190
In fact, Guyana was one of the countries which
used to benefit from PetroCaribe, an initiative

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:42.730
by Hugo Chavez that was supplying cheap, high
quality, oil to those countries which were

00:05:42.730 --> 00:05:44.080
deemed "friends".

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:49.450
But it all changed when, in May 11th 2005,
the left-wing government of the People's Progressive

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:54.830
Party lost the general elections to a coalition
headed by the new president David Granger,

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:59.500
a man who was closer to Washington and who
decided to end, once and for all, the claims

00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:00.500
coming from Venezuela.

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:15.460
At that moment, the long ignored conflict
defrosted and things started to heat up.

00:06:15.460 --> 00:06:22.890
The conflict is today in hands of the United
Nations.

00:06:22.890 --> 00:06:27.430
But, whatever the solution might be (if there
is any) it’s important to be aware of this

00:06:27.430 --> 00:06:34.800
threat to the potentially prosperous future
of Guyana.

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:38.590
RACIAL CONFLICT
Another important risk is in the recurrent

00:06:38.590 --> 00:06:43.210
racial conflict in Guyana, which is a continuous
presence in the country’s media.

00:06:43.210 --> 00:06:48.410
Guyana is a complex country demographically:
around 50% of its population is of Indian

00:06:48.410 --> 00:06:53.610
origin while 40% is of African origin.

00:06:53.610 --> 00:06:59.330
These two big groups are not exactly on friendly
terms.

00:06:59.330 --> 00:07:04.740
In fact, the black minority claims that, for
years, the Indian majority has obtained privileges

00:07:04.740 --> 00:07:07.069
from the government and always got their way.

00:07:07.069 --> 00:07:09.700
This has triggered recurrent waves of violence.

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:11.820
Luckily, the situation seems to have improved.

00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:16.970
In fact, the winning coalition government
is quite multiracial.

00:07:16.970 --> 00:07:23.310
However, there is still the possibility that
further internal conflict will flare up.

00:07:23.310 --> 00:07:27.230
In any case, not only does this new government
have a great opportunity to overcome decades

00:07:27.230 --> 00:07:32.010
of conflicts once and for all, but it was
also elected to fight violence and corruption

00:07:32.010 --> 00:07:36.710
in the country - something that Guyana certainly
needs - being one the most corrupt countries

00:07:36.710 --> 00:07:39.550
in the world according to Transparency International.

00:07:39.550 --> 00:07:43.860
So the new government has quite a few major
tasks ahead of them... oil exportation as

00:07:43.860 --> 00:07:47.260
well as a fight against corruption and criminality
in the country.

00:07:47.260 --> 00:07:51.669
The thing is, if they achieve their goals,
Guyana will attract great attention and may

00:07:51.669 --> 00:07:58.590
become the richest country in South America,
if they use their resources well.

00:07:58.590 --> 00:08:01.199
But will that happen?

00:08:01.199 --> 00:08:02.590
That is the big question...

00:08:02.590 --> 00:08:04.210
So what do you think?

00:08:04.210 --> 00:08:10.630
Will Guyana be able to successfully take advantage
of their newly discovered oil?

00:08:10.630 --> 00:08:12.650
What position should Venezuela adopt?

